# XSH dladdr()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Dl_info_t is the type the standard names (a system header that only knows Dl_info does not build this test;
# the module states the standard). Only addresses of symbols found with dlsym() on the program handle are used,
# with the null address as the one address that is in no mapped object.

assertion  XSH.dladdr.001
anchor     functions/dladdr.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/dladdr.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       dladdr() of the address dlsym() gave for getpid() returns non-zero
           with dli_fname a non-empty pathname, dli_fbase at or below the
           address, dli_sname non-null and dli_saddr equal to the address.
note       The object has a symbol table, since dlsym() found getpid in it.
test       t/001-function.c

assertion  XSH.dladdr.002
anchor     functions/dladdr.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       dladdr() of the null address, which lies in no mapped object, returns
           0.
test       t/002-null.c

assertion  XSH.dladdr.003
anchor     functions/dladdr.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/dladdr.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       dladdr() of the address dlsym() gave for the data object environ
           returns non-zero with dli_sname non-null and dli_saddr equal to the
           address.
test       t/003-data.c

assertion  XSH.dladdr.004
anchor     functions/dladdr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       dladdr() of an address one byte into getpid() returns non-zero, names
           the same object (pathname and base) as for its first byte, and reports
           a symbol whose address is not above the address asked.
test       t/004-inside.c
